---
source: tests/cli.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stdout).replace(\"multiplexer-driver.exe\",\n\"multiplexer-driver\")"
---
Set and clear workspace tags.

Prints {"workspace_id":…,"tags":{…}} with the tags as they are now. Keys match [A-Za-z0-9_-]+. At least one pair or --clear is required.

Example: multiplexer-driver --harness herdr workspace tag w1 project=x --clear old

Usage: multiplexer-driver workspace tag [OPTIONS] <WORKSPACE> [PAIRS]...

Arguments:
  <WORKSPACE>
          Workspace ID

  [PAIRS]...
          key=value pairs to set

Options:
      --clear <CLEAR>
          Keys to remove (repeatable)

      --harness <HARNESS>
          Harness to drive. Required for workspace, pane, and raw

          Possible values:
          - tmux:  tmux
          - herdr: Herdr
          - cmux:  cmux (macOS)
          - tuios: tuios
          - hc:    Herdr desktop app core (hc)
          
          [env: MULTIPLEXER_DRIVER_HARNESS=]

      --session <SESSION>
          Harness server to use: a Herdr session name, a tmux -L socket name, a cmux socket path, a tuios session name, or an hc session name (`HC_SESSION`). Unset uses the ambient server
          
          [env: MULTIPLEXER_DRIVER_SESSION=]

      --pretty
          Indent single-object output. Lists stay JSON Lines

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Diagnostics level on stderr: debug, info, warn, or error
          
          [env: RUST_LOG=]
          [default: warn]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
